{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SHfiH1zan6FJNU7ctdwKBZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"latest Node.js LTS major version 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Node.js 26 Released: What's New | InMotion Hosting\",\"url\":\"https://www.inmotionhosting.com/support/news/nodejs-v26-released/\"},{\"title\":\"Node.js Moves to One Major Release Per Year, Starting with Node 27 - InfoQ\",\"url\":\"https://www.infoq.com/news/2026/06/nodejs-release-changes/\"},{\"title\":\"Node.js — Node.js Releases\",\"url\":\"https://nodejs.org/en/about/previous-releases\"},{\"title\":\"Node.js — Node.js 26.0.0 (Current)\",\"url\":\"https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release/v26.0.0\"},{\"title\":\"Node.js — Evolving the Node.js Release Schedule\",\"url\":\"https://nodejs.org/en/blog/announcements/evolving-the-nodejs-release-schedule\"},{\"title\":\"Node.js | endoflife.date\",\"url\":\"https://endoflife.date/nodejs\"},{\"title\":\"Node.js v26 Is Here: What Actually Changed\",\"url\":\"https://nodesource.com/blog/nodejs-v26-is-here\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - nodejs/Release: Node.js Release Working Group · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nodejs/release\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · nodejs/node\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nodejs/node/releases\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the latest Node.js LTS major version in 2026:\n\n## Current LTS Status\n\nNode.js 24 is the current Active LTS release and Node.js 22 is in Maintenance LTS.\n\n## Node.js 26 Release\n\nNode.js 26 was released on May 5, 2026, as the new Current release in the Node.js long-term support (LTS) cycle. However, Node.js 26 launched as a Current release, not a Long-Term Support (LTS) release. After roughly six months as Current, it will transition to Active LTS status, with the official release post stating that Node.js 26 will enter LTS in October 2026.\n\n## Future Release Schedule Changes\n\nNode.js will change its release schedule starting with version 27 in October 2026, moving from two major releases per year to one. All releases will become Long-Term Support (LTS), removing the distinction between odd and even versions.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fff3c0d5-374e-40ad-a082-86d4d0e0e883","uuid":"96139baa-3eb7-433a-bc38-5c5c936a7896","timestamp":"2026-06-10T06:14:20.241Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"latest Node.js LTS major version 2026","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Q1echGtL4kTxGXh9dJ3U5Z","content":[{"title":"Node.js 26 Released: What's New | InMotion Hosting","url":"https://www.inmotionhosting.com/support/news/nodejs-v26-released/"},{"title":"Node.js Moves to One Major Release Per Year, Starting with Node 27 - InfoQ","url":"https://www.infoq.com/news/2026/06/nodejs-release-changes/"},{"title":"Node.js — Node.js Releases","url":"https://nodejs.org/en/about/previous-releases"},{"title":"Node.js — Node.js 26.0.0 (Current)","url":"https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release/v26.0.0"},{"title":"Node.js — Evolving the Node.js Release Schedule","url":"https://nodejs.org/en/blog/announcements/evolving-the-nodejs-release-schedule"},{"title":"Node.js | endoflife.date","url":"https://endoflife.date/nodejs"},{"title":"Node.js v26 Is Here: What Actually Changed","url":"https://nodesource.com/blog/nodejs-v26-is-here"},{"title":"GitHub - nodejs/Release: Node.js Release Working Group · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/nodejs/release"},{"title":"Releases · nodejs/node","url":"https://github.com/nodejs/node/releases"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about the latest Node.js LTS major version in 2026:\n\n## Current LTS Status\n\nNode.js 24 is the current Active LTS release and Node.js 22 is in Maintenance LTS.\n\n## Node.js 26 Release\n\nNode.js 26 was released on May 5, 2026, as the new Current release in the Node.js long-term support (LTS) cycle. However, Node.js 26 launched as a Current release, not a Long-Term Support (LTS) release. After roughly six months as Current, it will transition to Active LTS status, with the official release post stating that Node.js 26 will enter LTS in October 2026.\n\n## Future Release Schedule Changes\n\nNode.js will change its release schedule starting with version 27 in October 2026, moving from two major releases per year to one. All releases will become Long-Term Support (LTS), removing the distinction between odd and even versions."],"durationSeconds":5.862712042000001,"searchCount":1}}
